WEBVTT

01:42.018 --> 01:46.940
AN OLD DRAGON'S WRATH

01:48.983 --> 01:50.652
Hey you.

01:51.152 --> 01:54.739
How about an energy drink
made just for carnivores?

01:54.823 --> 01:57.951
I've got plenty of energy, thanks.

01:58.034 --> 02:03.373
Hey now, don't be shy.
How about a free sample?

02:05.375 --> 02:08.837
No, thanks. I...

02:15.760 --> 02:18.012
<i>This oughta get him addicted to meat.</i>

02:30.859 --> 02:32.527
Sorry, sorry!

02:32.610 --> 02:35.196
I slept in my underwear yesterday,
must've caught a cold.

02:37.073 --> 02:39.742
Hey, that energy drink.

02:40.285 --> 02:42.954
It's made with herbivore blood
and bones, right?

02:45.248 --> 02:46.624
None for me, thanks.

02:47.584 --> 02:48.585
Bye.

02:49.335 --> 02:52.088
- Wait.
- What the hell?

02:53.965 --> 02:57.886
<i>Just walk it off. It's not worth it.
Keep your nose out of trouble.</i>

02:58.761 --> 03:02.974
<i>- This is just how the adult world is.</i>
- You know that's not true, Legoshi.

03:05.226 --> 03:09.022
You devoured my meat
to bring a killer to justice.

03:09.105 --> 03:13.109
Will you really forgive
this crude cruelty so easily?

03:14.694 --> 03:17.280
Show them your anger, Legoshi.

03:20.617 --> 03:22.744
<i>If that's what Louis says...</i>

03:25.330 --> 03:27.332
What do you want?

03:27.415 --> 03:30.919
I ate my friend's meat while he was alive.

03:32.545 --> 03:35.673
I only react to the meat
of living herbivores.

03:35.757 --> 03:39.719
And I truly want to coexist
with those living herbivores.

03:39.802 --> 03:41.846
What the hell are you talking about?

03:41.930 --> 03:48.811
Have you ever thought about the lives
of the herbivores inside that drink?

03:48.895 --> 03:49.896
What?

03:49.979 --> 03:53.524
Why should I?
We've all gotta live true to ourselves!

04:01.866 --> 04:03.743
<i>For the sake of herbivores...</i>

04:04.535 --> 04:06.162
<i>For the sake of herbivores!</i>

04:08.164 --> 04:10.291
What's with that creepy smile?

04:16.130 --> 04:20.510
<i>For the sake of herbivores,
I have to live true to myself.</i>

04:49.414 --> 04:53.835
<i>My fangs are bared.
My body is thrashing. I can't stop!</i>

04:53.918 --> 04:55.253
Stop, please!

04:56.337 --> 04:57.797
I won't sell it anymore!

04:59.090 --> 05:00.216
I can't hear you.

05:04.721 --> 05:09.267
<i>I have to crush all of them.
For the sake of herbivores!</i>

05:12.395 --> 05:13.563
Enough already!

05:14.480 --> 05:20.445
<i>My entire body is screaming.
I want to live true to myself!</i>

05:31.831 --> 05:33.041
Run!

05:34.500 --> 05:35.877
You there! Stop!

05:37.837 --> 05:40.548
Wait! Stop there!

05:43.593 --> 05:46.471
SHISHI-GUMI

05:46.554 --> 05:51.601
Screw this. Why are we the ones
who have to collect the money?

05:52.101 --> 05:57.440
Whatever. At least we can get away
from that creepy boss of ours.

05:59.317 --> 06:00.359
Hey. Over here.

06:03.821 --> 06:06.449
How long were you planning
on making us wait?

06:06.532 --> 06:07.742
Take this for now.

06:09.535 --> 06:11.079
This ain't nearly enough.

06:11.162 --> 06:14.165
This isn't what we agreed on.

06:14.248 --> 06:15.291
What do you mean?

06:15.374 --> 06:17.168
The Kines!

06:17.668 --> 06:23.508
You said just one sniff would do it,
but that wolf kid wasn't affected at all.

06:25.176 --> 06:26.594
A carnivore?

06:26.677 --> 06:28.596
That's weird.

06:28.679 --> 06:29.806
Then he...

06:29.889 --> 06:34.310
He went on about avenging the herbivores
who were sacrificed for the ingredients

06:34.393 --> 06:35.394
and went crazy on us.

06:36.270 --> 06:39.232
<i>That little punk.
He won't get away with this.</i>

06:39.315 --> 06:42.276
Think we should tell the boss?

06:44.695 --> 06:46.823
- Hey!
- Just let me off the hook this once!

06:59.418 --> 07:00.878
Okay, everyone.

07:00.962 --> 07:04.757
With the school's new segregation policy
starting this year,

07:04.841 --> 07:07.260
coed clubs will be banned.

07:08.052 --> 07:12.807
So today, we're here to talk about
how to go forward with the drama club.

07:12.890 --> 07:14.350
Let's hear your opinions.

07:14.433 --> 07:19.230
Hey, who made you the boss?
You can't order us around.

07:19.313 --> 07:20.523
It looks good on you.

07:20.606 --> 07:21.941
Shut up!

07:22.024 --> 07:23.943
Yes, please be quiet.

07:24.444 --> 07:28.364
Louis chose Bill
to be club leader this year.

07:28.448 --> 07:29.991
HAVE SEPARATE CLUBS
OR SUSPEND THE CLUB

07:30.074 --> 07:33.494
Then I vote for suspending the club.

07:34.495 --> 07:37.999
Louis stood up to the devourer
all by himself,

07:38.082 --> 07:40.793
and he chose you, a carnivore,
to be club leader, right?

07:40.877 --> 07:44.213
So, screw this half-baked compromise
of splitting up.

07:44.297 --> 07:46.591
I say we band together
and protest the school.

07:47.091 --> 07:48.676
You've changed.

07:49.177 --> 07:53.473
But if we do that,
we might lose this club forever.

07:55.057 --> 07:55.892
That's true.

07:55.975 --> 07:59.562
But we've worked together just fine
all these years.

07:59.645 --> 08:02.398
We can't give up now.
We have to try to persuade the school.

08:02.482 --> 08:05.526
We worked together just fine?
Do you really think so?

08:06.861 --> 08:10.865
I hate to say it,
but we had two incidents in one year.

08:12.325 --> 08:15.620
Can you really say we got along?

08:15.703 --> 08:17.038
What do you mean?

08:17.121 --> 08:18.998
Am I wrong?

08:19.499 --> 08:24.170
The decision to segregate the school
was because of the incident we caused.

08:24.253 --> 08:27.465
Why do you always
make everything the carnivores' fault?

08:27.548 --> 08:29.467
I didn't say that.

08:29.550 --> 08:31.636
Everyone, calm down.

08:34.555 --> 08:36.015
What do you think, Juno?

08:38.601 --> 08:39.727
I...

08:41.479 --> 08:42.980
"Coexistence and mutual prosperity."

08:44.649 --> 08:46.901
The most important thing right now

08:46.984 --> 08:51.239
is not to let the spirit
of coexistence and mutual prosperity die.

08:54.242 --> 08:58.955
The reason we carnivores and herbivores
worked together in the drama club

08:59.038 --> 09:02.583
was to embody that idea, wasn't it?

09:03.376 --> 09:07.797
If we all have that ambition,
we'll be together even when we're apart.

09:08.381 --> 09:12.218
Even if we end up splitting up the club,

09:12.301 --> 09:17.181
I plan to carry on the club's ambitions.
Louis's ambitions.

09:17.682 --> 09:19.016
Good point.

09:19.100 --> 09:20.351
Well said, Juno.

09:20.434 --> 09:23.563
Well, I'll be leaving the club, then.

09:24.730 --> 09:30.444
Didn't you hear me?
Thanks for the fun... six months or so.

09:31.654 --> 09:34.699
I don't believe in
long distance relationships.

09:35.366 --> 09:39.161
"Our hearts are one even when apart."
That's garbage.

09:40.371 --> 09:45.960
I learned something while working together
with carnivores in this club.

09:47.461 --> 09:49.463
Sharp claws and fangs...

09:49.964 --> 09:54.093
These things I don't have,
they give me the creeps.

09:55.261 --> 09:57.096
They're straight-up freaky!

09:57.179 --> 10:01.809
Even so, there's no point
in being here if we're separated.

10:02.393 --> 10:03.394
I quit.

10:05.563 --> 10:07.982
Take care, everyone.

10:13.946 --> 10:14.947
Don't say it.

10:16.574 --> 10:19.702
Don't say, "If only Louis were here."

10:22.330 --> 10:23.414
Right.

10:44.894 --> 10:45.895
Huh?

10:49.231 --> 10:50.232
Legoshi!

10:51.442 --> 10:52.443
Haru!

10:56.489 --> 10:57.490
What's wrong?

10:58.491 --> 11:01.535
What is it? What's wrong?

11:02.244 --> 11:03.496
You look so good.

11:04.664 --> 11:06.791
Don't be a creep.

11:08.459 --> 11:11.295
No work today? We didn't make plans.

11:11.379 --> 11:13.089
I know, but...

11:14.840 --> 11:16.384
Hey, Legoshi.

11:17.051 --> 11:19.512
I won't ask you about that scar, okay?

11:20.262 --> 11:23.057
This is nothing. I just fell.

11:24.642 --> 11:29.730
Actually, I came here
to tell you something.

11:30.731 --> 11:32.733
I want to be honest with you.

11:34.735 --> 11:35.861
Listen.

11:37.488 --> 11:40.282
Well... there's...

11:41.867 --> 11:43.744
something I haven't told you about.

11:44.412 --> 11:46.580
- What?
- You see, I...

11:47.123 --> 11:48.124
Haru!

11:48.749 --> 11:50.292
Hey! Wolf!

11:50.376 --> 11:55.506
- Thanks for picking up my change! Bye!
- Wait... What?

11:59.260 --> 12:01.554
You're early, Dad.

12:01.637 --> 12:03.055
<i>Dad?</i>

12:03.722 --> 12:06.684
You still don't have a bus card?

12:06.767 --> 12:11.522
The new school IDs aren't in yet.

12:11.605 --> 12:14.275
- I see.
<i>- I couldn't even say hi.</i>

12:15.568 --> 12:18.988
<i>He'd never accept a carnivore...</i>

12:29.665 --> 12:36.630
MAIMAI MILK

12:40.509 --> 12:42.803
You listening?
You'd do well to remember this.

12:43.387 --> 12:49.101
This society exists
due to the generosity of herbivores.

12:54.815 --> 12:56.901
And because of me.

12:57.568 --> 13:00.905
Forgive me.
I'll make sure they leave by 8:00.

13:02.364 --> 13:03.616
This is your last chance.

13:03.699 --> 13:06.410
- Of... of course.
- Thank you.

13:06.494 --> 13:11.207
I should have come sooner.
I didn't know you were suffering.

13:11.290 --> 13:12.500
Forgive me.

13:12.583 --> 13:16.545
- Thank you for your help.
- Thank you so much!

13:21.592 --> 13:22.718
Yahya.

13:23.469 --> 13:24.887
How did it go?

13:25.429 --> 13:26.263
Well.

13:26.764 --> 13:31.143
The Kines dealers' mark,
the gray wolf, caused quite the commotion.

13:32.186 --> 13:33.771
There's no doubt about it.

13:33.854 --> 13:38.108
It's the same pup
that ate his friend's leg.

13:38.901 --> 13:42.780
As I expected. Truly an interesting case.

13:43.614 --> 13:46.367
A wannabe vigilante, perhaps?

13:46.450 --> 13:50.746
Even though this city's already got
a great Beastar like you, Mr. Yahya.

13:50.829 --> 13:55.876
There's only so much
this old horse can do to protect the city.

13:55.960 --> 13:57.294
But...

13:57.378 --> 14:00.214
I do thank you for helping me.

14:01.173 --> 14:04.009
Until we get rid of that drink,

14:04.093 --> 14:07.638
the perfect world we strive for
is still a long ways off.

14:09.598 --> 14:13.978
<i>This horse's vision
is just shy of perfect.</i>

14:15.187 --> 14:17.565
<i>Horses have 350-degree vision.</i>

14:17.648 --> 14:21.026
<i>If I could only see another 10 degrees,</i>

14:21.110 --> 14:24.613
<i>I could observe every nook
and cranny of society.</i>

14:26.031 --> 14:29.201
<i>This never-ending fight against crime.</i>

14:30.536 --> 14:31.704
<i>If only.</i>

14:31.787 --> 14:35.082
<i>If only I had the 360-degree vision
I did back then.</i>

14:36.125 --> 14:38.460
<i>I could end it once and for all.</i>

14:40.296 --> 14:42.506
<i>But, my old friend...</i>

14:44.091 --> 14:46.051
<i>You've made that impossible, you beast.</i>

14:47.511 --> 14:51.265
<i>A perfect power. A perfect society.</i>

14:51.891 --> 14:55.644
<i>And a once perfect trust.</i>

14:56.729 --> 14:58.772
<i>A mere 10 degrees.</i>

14:58.856 --> 15:00.983
<i>A whole 10 degrees.</i>

15:01.734 --> 15:02.651
<i>Gosha!</i>

15:29.094 --> 15:33.933
<i>Every time I get closer to Haru,
it feels like we grow further apart.</i>

15:35.643 --> 15:40.856
<i>Why are interspecies relationships
so difficult to maintain?</i>

15:47.863 --> 15:50.366
<i>A lizard. Payback for yesterday?</i>

16:32.324 --> 16:36.495
<i>A Komodo dragon's venom
doesn't affect their family members.</i>

16:37.329 --> 16:40.958
Legoshi! How ya been?

16:41.041 --> 16:43.877
That was some greeting, Grandpa.

16:43.961 --> 16:47.798
What's the big deal?
It's just your grandpa's venom.

16:48.298 --> 16:51.468
You're my only grandson, after all!

16:52.302 --> 16:53.303
Grandpa.

16:55.264 --> 16:58.392
<i>The venom that would kill any other animal</i>

16:59.184 --> 17:01.145
<i>tastes sweet and bitter to me.</i>

17:01.645 --> 17:03.564
<i>Like marmalade.</i>

17:05.607 --> 17:08.318
<i>You like french fries, right, Legoshi?</i>

17:09.695 --> 17:11.155
Well, sure I do.

17:11.238 --> 17:13.240
Great. Let's go get some.

17:14.158 --> 17:15.200
Okay.

17:18.162 --> 17:23.500
<i>I liked them when I was kid,
but that was a long time ago.</i>

17:26.128 --> 17:27.671
Well, at night...

17:29.840 --> 17:31.175
<i>This is fine.</i>

17:31.842 --> 17:34.219
<i>We don't have to talk
about anything special.</i>

17:35.971 --> 17:37.181
Why don't we sit here?

17:38.390 --> 17:40.309
It's not like it's busy.

17:40.392 --> 17:41.977
We don't need to sit over there.

17:44.188 --> 17:45.814
But...

17:45.898 --> 17:50.944
<i>Legoshi, have you forgotten our rule?</i>

17:51.862 --> 17:53.030
<i>When you go out to eat,</i>

17:53.113 --> 17:56.950
<i>always choose a table in the back,
out of sight.</i>

17:57.785 --> 18:02.247
<i>Being a venomous Komodo dragon,</i>

18:02.331 --> 18:04.875
<i>I was the victim of all kinds of bigotry.</i>

18:05.542 --> 18:06.668
<i>But you...</i>

18:07.795 --> 18:09.880
<i>I've always thought it was strange.</i>

18:11.215 --> 18:14.885
We weren't doing anything wrong.
Why did we have to sit in the back?

18:14.968 --> 18:16.512
Well...

18:17.638 --> 18:18.806
Go ahead.

18:27.689 --> 18:28.941
Aren't you hungry?

18:32.611 --> 18:34.988
I'm sorry for quitting school
without telling you.

18:35.989 --> 18:37.324
That's why you're here, right?

18:38.450 --> 18:40.244
What happened?

18:40.327 --> 18:42.996
You've got those scars on your face.

18:43.080 --> 18:45.332
- Why didn't you talk to m--
- I couldn't.

18:45.916 --> 18:49.962
You couldn't help Mom
when she was in trouble, either.

18:50.045 --> 18:53.799
- Legoshi.
- I'm grateful to you for raising me.

18:54.383 --> 18:56.885
But I can take care of myself now.

18:58.220 --> 18:59.972
What do you wanna eat?

19:00.055 --> 19:02.307
What did I always get here?

19:02.391 --> 19:04.143
How the hell should I know?

19:05.269 --> 19:08.105
You're right. I won't deny that.

19:08.188 --> 19:11.108
But I just want you to remember this.

19:11.191 --> 19:13.610
What I taught you...

19:14.278 --> 19:16.363
What I always wanted you to know...

19:16.446 --> 19:18.907
The doctrine of pacifism. Right?

19:19.908 --> 19:21.034
I remember.

19:23.078 --> 19:24.121
I see.

19:27.291 --> 19:28.292
Hey.

19:28.876 --> 19:31.879
Who let a venom user
take all the good seats?

19:31.962 --> 19:33.755
It's a full house, Gramps.

19:33.839 --> 19:37.926
Move it before you poison
the whole restaurant.

19:39.428 --> 19:40.470
Excuse me?

19:43.682 --> 19:45.434
Let's move, Legoshi.

19:45.517 --> 19:46.518
Legoshi!

19:46.602 --> 19:49.479
I didn't quite hear you.

19:50.189 --> 19:53.400
Do you actually think his venom
is transmitted through the air?

19:53.483 --> 19:54.526
That's ridiculous.

19:55.819 --> 19:59.448
Watch your mouth, mutt. You wanna go?

19:59.531 --> 20:01.200
I'm up for it if you are.

20:01.283 --> 20:02.284
Legoshi.

20:08.957 --> 20:10.709
All right, that's enough.

20:11.376 --> 20:14.213
There are other customers here.

20:14.296 --> 20:16.673
I'm going to have to ask you to stop.

20:18.675 --> 20:21.011
You're lucky the owner's a reptile.

20:21.929 --> 20:23.764
Screw this place.

20:23.847 --> 20:25.098
Just you wait, assholes.

20:28.227 --> 20:29.686
Give me a break.

20:29.770 --> 20:32.522
Excuse me, do you have ant shakes?

20:32.606 --> 20:33.690
Sure do.

20:34.441 --> 20:36.401
- Great, I'll take a medium.
<i>- Legoshi.</i>

20:36.985 --> 20:38.946
- Coming right up.
<i>- You...</i>

20:48.664 --> 20:50.874
We're supposed to be pacifists!

20:50.958 --> 20:53.377
- You don't get it at all.
- Grandpa!

20:53.460 --> 20:56.380
I couldn't just let them walk all over us.

20:56.463 --> 20:59.341
I can't sit back and watch
like when I was a kid.

20:59.424 --> 21:01.426
You are a kid!

21:02.803 --> 21:03.804
Listen up.

21:03.887 --> 21:07.474
To survive in this world,
you need to remember one more thing.

21:07.557 --> 21:10.060
You need to let things go.

21:10.143 --> 21:12.771
That's the only way
to stay out of trouble.

21:22.114 --> 21:23.282
Hey.

21:23.365 --> 21:26.243
You really made us
look like idiots back there.

21:27.077 --> 21:31.415
Walking through a dark alley like this,

21:31.498 --> 21:33.834
you should know
what's gonna happen to you.

21:33.917 --> 21:35.335
You couple of freaks!

21:40.632 --> 21:42.759
Don't touch him!

21:46.972 --> 21:49.599
You've got some soft feathers.

21:49.683 --> 21:52.311
Be grateful I didn't poison you.

21:52.394 --> 21:53.520
You bastard!

22:00.027 --> 22:02.946
A good old blood bath. It's been a while.

22:05.073 --> 22:07.409
<i>Grandpa...</i>

22:08.201 --> 22:09.661
<i>Who are you?</i>

23:36.915 --> 23:41.920
Subtitle translation by: Thomas Grathwol
